.\" Man page for crypto_tool(1)
.\" Generated from COMPLETE_CLI_OPTIONS_AND_ARGUMENTS.md
.TH CRYPTO_TOOL 1 "November 2026" "ETL Madness Flow" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
crypto_tool \- AES-256-GCM encryption, digital signature, and keypair utility for Flow
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crypto_tool
.RI [ options ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B crypto_tool
is a standalone, zero-dependency cryptographic command-line utility for the ETL Madness Flow ecosystem.
It provides authenticated AES-256-GCM symmetric encryption and decryption, digital signature creation and verification across OpenSSL (RSA, ECDSA, Ed25519), OpenPGP, and PKCS#7/CMS formats, unified signed envelopes
.RB ( FLOWSIGNED:v1:... ),
and asymmetric keypair and self-signed X.509 certificate generation.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Operation & I/O Options
.TP
.BI \-action " op"
Cryptographic operation to perform:
.B encrypt
(default),
.BR decrypt ,
.BR gen-key ,
.BR sign ,
.BR verify ,
or
.BR gen-keypair .
.TP
.B \-gen-key
Shortcut flag equivalent to
.BR "\-action gen-key" .
Generates a 256-bit cryptographically secure symmetric key.
.TP
.BI \-in " path"
Input file path.
Use
.B \-
or omit to read from standard input
.RI ( stdin ).
.TP
.BI \-out " path"
Output file path.
Use
.B \-
or omit to write to standard output
.RI ( stdout ).
Output files containing secret keys are written with
.B 0600
permissions.
.SS Symmetric Encryption & Decryption Options
.TP
.BI \-secure-key " key" "\fR, \fP\-key " key
Passphrase or raw key for AES-256-GCM encryption or decryption.
Emits a security warning to
.I stderr
because command-line flags are visible in system process listings; falls back to
.B FLOW_SECURE_KEY
or
.BR SECURE_KEY .
.TP
.BI \-key-file " path"
Path to a file containing the symmetric encryption/decryption key or passphrase.
Preferred over
.B \-secure-key
to avoid exposing secrets in process tables.
.TP
.B \-binary
Output raw binary ciphertext or raw ASN.1 signature bytes instead of the default text-safe armored envelope
.RB ( FLOWENC:v1:...
or
.BR FLOWSIG:v1:... ).
.SS Digital Signing Options
.TP
.BI \-sig-type " format"
Digital signature format for
.BR "\-action sign" :
.B openssl
(default; RSA, ECDSA, or Ed25519),
.B pgp
(OpenPGP), or
.B pkcs7
(CMS / PKCS#7).
.TP
.BI \-private-key " path" "\fR, \fP\-priv " path
Private key file path (PEM or OpenPGP format) used to generate digital signatures.
.TP
.BI \-passphrase " str"
Passphrase for decrypting password-protected private keys (PKCS#1, PKCS#8, or OpenPGP).
.TP
.BI \-cert " path"
X.509 certificate file path (PEM or DER format).
Required when creating PKCS#7 signatures
.RB ( "\-sig-type pkcs7" )
and supported for certificate-based verification.
.TP
.B \-wrap
Wrap both the digital signature and input payload into a single self-contained
.B FLOWSIGNED:v1:...
envelope, eliminating the need for detached signature files.
.SS Signature Verification Options
.TP
.BI \-signature " path" "\fR, \fP\-sig " path
Detached signature file path for
.BR "\-action verify" .
When omitted, companion files
.IR <in>.sig ,
.IR <in>.asc ,
or
.I <in>.p7s
are checked automatically.
.TP
.BI \-public-key " path" "\fR, \fP\-pub " path
Public key file path (PEM or OpenPGP format) for signature verification.
.TP
.BI \-ca-cert " path"
Root or intermediate CA certificate file path used to validate certificate chains during PKCS#7 or X.509 verification.
.TP
.BI \-keyring " path"
OpenPGP armored public keyring file path for OpenPGP/GPG signature verification.
.SS Keypair & Certificate Generation Options
.TP
.BI \-keypair-type " type"
Asymmetric keypair algorithm for
.BR "\-action gen-keypair" :
.B rsa
(default),
.B ecdsa
(P-256),
.BR ed25519 ,
or
.B pgp
(aliases:
.BR gpg ,
.BR openpgp ).
.TP
.BI \-bits " n"
Bit length for RSA keypair generation (for example,
.BR 2048 ,
.BR 3072 ,
or
.BR 4096 ).
Default:
.BR 2048 .
.TP
.BI \-out-priv " path"
Output file path for the generated private key (restricted to
.B 0600
permissions).
Default:
.IR private_key.pem .
.TP
.BI \-out-pub " path"
Output file path for the generated public key (written with
.B 0644
permissions).
Default:
.IR public_key.pem .
.TP
.BI \-out-cert " path"
Optional output path to generate a self-signed X.509 certificate valid for 365 days during keypair generation.
.TP
.BI \-cn " name"
Common Name
.RB ( CN )
embedded in the generated X.509 certificate or OpenPGP user identity.
Default:
.IR "Flow Code Signer" .
.SH SECRET RESOLUTION PRECEDENCE
Symmetric keys and passphrases are resolved in the following order:
.IP 1. 4
.BI \-key-file " path"
.IP 2. 4
.BI \-secure-key " key"
(or
.BR \-key )
.IP 3. 4
.B FLOW_SECURE_KEY
environment variable
.IP 4. 4
.B SECURE_KEY
environment variable
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FLOW_SECURE_KEY
Primary symmetric passphrase or key for AES-256-GCM encryption/decryption.
.TP
.B SECURE_KEY
Fallback symmetric passphrase or key if
.B FLOW_SECURE_KEY
is unset.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (operation or signature verification succeeded).
.TP
.B 1
Failure (invalid arguments, missing key, decryption authentication failure, or signature verification failure).
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate a 256-bit symmetric key, encrypt an XML pipeline, and decrypt it:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
crypto_tool \-gen-key \-out master.key
crypto_tool \-action encrypt \-in pipeline.xml \-out pipeline.xml.enc \-key-file master.key
crypto_tool \-action decrypt \-in pipeline.xml.enc \-out pipeline.xml \-key-file master.key
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate an RSA keypair with a self-signed X.509 certificate:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
crypto_tool \-action gen-keypair \-keypair-type rsa \-bits 2048 \\
  \-out-priv release_priv.pem \-out-pub release_pub.pem \-out-cert release_cert.pem \\
  \-cn "Production Code Signer"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create and verify a unified
.B FLOWSIGNED:v1:...
package (encrypt-then-sign):
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
crypto_tool \-action sign \-in pipeline.xml.enc \-out pipeline.xml.signed \\
  \-private-key release_priv.pem \-wrap
crypto_tool \-action verify \-in pipeline.xml.signed \\
  \-public-key release_pub.pem \-out verified_pipeline.xml.enc
.fi
.RE
